    "scientific_summary": "Phenotypic variables alone achieve substantial site decoding accuracy well above the 19.91% majority baseline, proving that demographic and behavioral distributions differ across clinical sites (e.g., pediatric vs adult sites, IQ inclusion thresholds, motion distributions). When connectomes are deconfounded by regressing out age, sex, FIQ, motion, and diagnosis strictly within training folds, site decoding remains well above chance. Crucially, this residual site predictability reflects broad 'site-associated information'\u2014including distinct recruitment protocols, imaging parameter variations (TR, TE, flip angle, voxel resolution), and scanner RF coils\u2014rather than purely isolated scanner hardware signatures."
